PERMITTED PURPOSES
================================================================================

The only permitted purpose for the software is any purpose that is not a 
commercial purpose.

This explicitly permits:
  • Inspecting, studying, and reviewing the source code and architecture.
  • Academic research, educational exploration, and instructional use.
  • Private experimentation, personal modifications, and local runs.
  • Non-commercial derivation and investigation development.

================================================================================
COMMERCIAL PURPOSES
================================================================================

A commercial purpose is any purpose that is intended or directed toward 
commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

This explicitly prohibits:
  • Selling ENIGMA as a standalone commercial product, service, or exhibit.
  • Modifying, remaking, rebranding, or repackaging ENIGMA and selling that 
    derivative work for commercial compensation.
  • Operating ENIGMA as a paid or subscription-based software-as-a-service (SaaS).
  • Distributing ENIGMA or derivatives thereof in exchange for any fee without 
    prior written authorization from the copyright holder.

